s explain variations in sale prices. Larger living areas generally tend to be associated with higher prices.\n","- **Neighborhood:** Average house prices vary across different neighborhoods.\n","- **Outlier Detection:** IQR and Z-score methods were used to identify unusual observations. Potential outliers were inspected and retained because they were not automatically considered data errors.\n","- **Data Quality:** Duplicate records, missing values, impossible year values, and negative area values were checked and addressed.\n","\n","## 3. Conclusion\n","\n","This project demonstrates how Exploratory Data Analysis can be used to understand a housing dataset through descriptive statistics, visualizations, correlation analysis, outlier detection, and data quality checks.\n","\n","The analysis provides useful insights into the relationship between house characteristics and sale prices. It also highlights the importance of cleaning and understanding data before drawing conclusions.\n","\n","## 4. Learning Outcomes\n","\n","- Learned to use Python libraries such as Pandas, NumPy, Matplotlib, and Seaborn.\n","- Understood numerical, categorical, and ordinal variables.\n","- Practised descriptive statistics and data visualization.\n","- Applied correlation, covariance, and outlier detection techniques.\n","- Learned how to identify and handle missing values and data quality issues.\n","\n","**Project Status: Exploratory Data Analysis Completed.**"],"metadata":{"id":"wKeHa7Yu2lXk"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"54QANYsI2gC5"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"tfITqsfx2f_w"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"qXAOoOB_2f8m"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"iOVHVyuc2f5d"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"ihNjaV9T2f2M"},"execution_count":null,"out